== About Me
I am an associate professor of EECS and Statistics at UC Berkeley. 

 Previously, I was a research scientist at Google Deepmind, member of the [https://www.math.ias.edu/sp/Optimization_Statistics_and_Theoretical_Machine_Learning IAS], and an associate professor at Princeton. Before that, I was a postdoc at UC Berkeley working with [http://www.cs.berkeley.edu/~jordan/ Michael I. Jordan]. I received my PhD at Stanford advised by [http://www.stanford.edu/~hastie Trevor Hastie] and [http://statweb.stanford.edu/~jtaylo/ Jonathan Taylor]. I received a BS in Mathematics from Duke University advised by [http://www.math.duke.edu/~mauro/ Mauro Maggioni].
I am a native of Cupertino, CA.\n



My research interests are broadly in
- Foundations of AI and Deep Learning [slides/beyond_ntk.pdf (slides)] [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vQsuF21tGQk&t=26s (video)]\n
- Representation Learning [slides/representation_learning_slides.pdf Slides] and  [https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1BA411E7t8?from=search&seid=15450836602360104202 Video].\n
- Foundations of Deep Reinforcement Learning [http://statisticalml.stat.columbia.edu/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/pg_tutorial.pdf (slides)] [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VRXRocjsR0E (video 1)] [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZHhzyCwUE1A (video 2)] \n

~~~
{Students, Visitors, and Postdocs}
Any email from prospective students, postdoc, or visitors, please include the string "filter_student" in the subject, else I will not receive your email; please use the gmail given above, not the Berkeley mail which I do not filter. I am recruiting *PhD students* and *postdoctoral scholars* starting in 2025 at Berkeley, please email me a CV apply. *Berkeley PhD students* interested in machine learning, statistics, or optimization research, please contact me.   \n

My current focus is on machine learning with a focus on foundations of AI, deep learning, representation learning, and deep reinforcement learning. I have lectured on the Foudations of Deep Learning at MIT [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vtsjtB6RamE&t=3s Video] and [slides/foundations_DL.pdf Slides]; my tutorial at the Simons Institute:  [slides/simons_tutorial_Overparam_opt_DL.pdf  Slides] and [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uC2IGoTE2u4&t=1162s Video]; and my tutorial at Machine Learning Summer School (MLSS 2021): [https://youtu.be/ukxzDErn06E Video] and [slides/beyond_ntk.pdf  Slides].

I have also given tutorials on Representation Learning at the Johns Hopkins Winter School and Beijing AI Institute; [slides/representation_learning_slides.pdf Slides] and  [https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1BA411E7t8?from=search&seid=15450836602360104202 Video]. 


I am also happy to host *visitors*. Summer visitors please contact me around February to schedule your visit. See a list of past visitors at [group.html here].
